This product includes software developed at OpenMMLab
(https://github.com/open-mmlab/mmdetection).

The `vfe/` package is a derivative work of MMDetection 2.19.1 and MMCV 1.3.17,
both licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. It reimplements the parts
of those projects that MAMBA and STPN use -- models, data pipeline, evaluator,
training loop, samplers, config system -- on plain PyTorch, so that neither mmcv
nor mmdet nor mmengine is imported at runtime. Structure, naming, defaults and
numerical behaviour deliberately follow the originals: the reimplementation is
checked against them tensor by tensor (see docs/parity.md).

Until version 2.0 this repository also vendored MMDetection 2.19.1 in full,
under `mmdet/`. That tree is preserved at the `v1.0.0` tag and carries its own
copyright notices.

`vfe/evaluation/vid_motion_iou.npz` is converted from the ImageNet VID
validation motion-IoU table published with Flow-Guided Feature Aggregation
(https://github.com/msracver/Flow-Guided-Feature-Aggregation), and is used by
the motion-based AP breakdown that the video object detection literature
reports.
